      "rationale": "an unmodelled action is refused rather than approximated, because a guessed cost basis is indistinguishable from a correct one downstream, and an ignored action leaves the ledger describing a security that no longer exists as recorded",
      "refused_by_name": {
        "CASH_IN_LIEU": "it realises a fractional position at a price the event does not state, so the realised amount would be invented",
        "MERGER": "the treatment depends on the exchange ratio, any cash component and whether the exchange is taxable; each decides a different cost basis for the surviving holding",
        "RETURN_OF_CAPITAL": "it reduces cost basis rather than being income, and treating it as a dividend would overstate income and understate every later realised gain",
        "RIGHTS_DISTRIBUTION": "the subscription price and whether the rights were exercised, sold or lapsed each produce a different outcome",
        "SPINOFF": "basis must be allocated between parent and child by relative fair value at distribution, which the event does not carry",
        "STOCK_DIVIDEND": "it resembles a split but is not always one; whether basis is reallocated depends on the character of the distribution",
        "SYMBOL_SUBSTITUTION": "a symbol change is display-only and already harmless here, since identity is `(kind, identity_id)` and never the ticker. A substitution that actually changes the security is a different security",
        "TENDER_OFFER": "the proration factor decides how much was actually tendered, and it is not known until after the offer closes"
      },
      "supported": {
        "CASH_DIVIDEND": "credited to cash as income, with cost basis untouched. Entitlement is the producer's responsibility: inferring it from current holdings would miss a position sold between the ex-date and the pay date and would credit one bought after it.",
        "SPLIT": "quantity scales by the ratio and total cost does not, so average cost moves by exactly the ratio and no gain or loss is created. A reverse split's fractional residue is recorded rather than rounded away."
      }
    },
